# `plans/evidence/` holds two different things under one path.
#
#   * The audit chain: the result JSON each spec writes, the freeze metadata
#     and the human rulings.  A release claim is checked against these, so
#     they stay tracked.
#   * Everything a re-run also produces: a screenshot for every step, per-run
#     server stdout, and older snapshots of the same spec keyed by build hash.
#     Replaying the suite regenerates them, and they were 97 MB of the 107 MB
#     this directory weighed.
#
# Ignoring the whole directory keeps the second kind from creeping back: an
# ignore rule does not apply to a path git already tracks, so the 172 audit
# files below stay, and each re-run overwrites them in place.  A new artifact
# that a document cites has to be re-included by an explicit `!` line, which
# is the only way it should ever become tracked.  0.0.3 ruled this split and
# never enforced it; the history is in plans/0.0.3-release-commit-plan.md §3.
plans/evidence/**
!plans/evidence/*.md
!plans/evidence/*.json
!plans/evidence/*.patch

# Release-prep exclusions (user ruling 2026-11-06)
/机制提炼/
plans/evidence/**/playwright-report/

# Operator review material from the project-audit pass (2026-11-09).  A local
# findings bundle, not a product artifact; it carries no build input.
/_审视/
